!! Command listener adapter for JSON files

We'll start defining a test class:

% ${changes:path=code/001-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsJsonAdapterTest.ombu}
[[[classDefinition=true
TestCase subclass: #EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsJsonAdapterTest
	instanceVariableNames: ''
	classVariableNames: ''
	package: 'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-Json-Tests'
]]]

It's a new package, so we need to make sure to add it to the baseline. Remember to right-click on it an choose "Promote as package", and then add the package to the repository in Iceberg.

% ${changes:path=code/002-BaselineOfPharoEDASettings_declarePackagesIn_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
declarePackagesIn: spec

	spec
		package: #'EDAS-Settings'
		with: [ spec requires: #( 'DeployUtils' ) ];
		package: #'EDAS-Settings-Tests'
		with: [ spec requires: #( 'EDAS-Settings' ) ];
		package: #'EDAS-Settings-Ports'
		with: [ spec requires: #( 'PharoEDACommon' ) ];
		package: #'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-InMemory'
		with: [ spec requires: #( 'PharoEDACommon' 'EDAS-Settings-Ports' ) ];
		package: #'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-EnvVars'
		with: [ spec requires: #( 'PharoEDACommon' 'EDAS-Settings-Ports' ) ];
		package: #'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-Json-Tests'
		with: [ spec requires: #( 'PharoEDACommon' 'EDAS-Settings-Ports' ) ];
		package: #'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-ByPriority' with: [
			spec requires:
					#( 'PharoEDACommon' 'EDAS-Settings-Ports' 'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-InMemory'
					   'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-EnvVars' ) ]
]]]

% ${changes:path=code/003-BaselineOfPharoEDASettings_declareGroupsIn_.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
declareGroupsIn: spec

	spec
		group: 'core'
		with:
			#( #'EDAS-Settings' #'EDAS-Settings-Ports' #'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-InMemory'
			   #'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-EnvVars'
			   #'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-ByPriority' );
		group: 'tests'
		with:
			#( #'EDAS-Settings-Tests' #'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-Json-Tests' );
		group: 'default' with: #( 'core' 'tests' )
]]]

Our first test would be simple:

% ${changes:path=code/004-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsJsonAdapterTest_testHost_localhost.ombu}
[[[methodDefinition=true
EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsJsonAdapterTest >> testHost_localhost

	| json dict tempFile commandListener |
	tempFile := FileReference
		            newTempFilePrefix:
		            'EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsJsonAdapterTest'
		            suffix: '.json'.
	commandListener := Dictionary new.
	commandListener at: 'host' put: 'localhost'.
	dict := Dictionary new.
	dict at: 'commandListener' put: commandListener.
	json := String streamContents: [ :stream |
		        (NeoJSONWriter on: stream)
			        asciiOnly: true;
			        nextPut: dict ].
	tempFile writeStreamDo: [ :s | s nextPutAll: json ].
	self
		assert:
			(EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsJsonAdapter fromFile: tempFile withApp: nil) host
			= 'localhost'
		description: 'Host parsing failed'
		resumable: true.
	tempFile delete
]]]

This test would trigger the dialog allowing you to create the new ==EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsJsonAdapter== class:

% ${changes:path=code/005-EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsJsonAdapter.ombu}
[[[classDefinition=true
Object subclass: #EDASStompTopicListenerSettingsJsonAdapter
    uses: EDASSettingsPort
	instanceVariableNames: 'host port user password timeout queue prefetchCount ack debug durable restartOnErrors errorStrategyName edaApplication'
	classVariableNames: ''
	package: 'EDAS-Settings-Adapters-Json'
]]]

